  "changelog": "**Major architecture and feature expansion for code-factory 1.0.1**\n\n- Introduced step_handlers layer with 7 dedicated handler modules for granular step management.\n- Expanded contracts with new files: step_outputs.py (TypedDict output types) and exceptions.py (unified exception definitions).\n- Middlewares enhanced with additional modules: pipeline_guard.py, saga_coordinator.py, and service_container.py for improved fault tolerance and DI.\n- Execution flow restructured: step handlers mapped to physical modules, improved compensating transactions, and state transitions now cover six states (success, failed, skipped, timed out, rolled back, running).\n- Self-test coverage expanded (17 test files, 174 test cases), and error handling now supports Saga compensation and atomic file writes.\n- skill-card.md removed; documentation and architecture diagrams updated to reflect the layered, handler-driven design.",
